1
00:00:02,070 --> 00:00:12,510
Molly, I need your special talent for handling special matters.

2
00:00:12,510 --> 00:00:15,470
Like what special matters?

3
00:00:15,470 --> 00:00:17,700
Well, I have a scheduling problem.

4
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:18,780
Yes?

5
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:22,230
I have three tonsillectomies set for Friday with Dr. Earl.

6
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:23,400
Yes?

7
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:26,890
I need to fit a fourth operation into his schedule.

8
00:00:26,890 --> 00:00:30,750
And ... I know you can do it.

9
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:32,210
Who's the patient?

10
00:00:32,210 --> 00:00:33,250
Carl Herrera.

11
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:34,810
The boy has infected tonsils,

12
00:00:34,810 --> 00:00:37,710
and we should remove them as soon as possible.

13
00:00:37,710 --> 00:00:39,480
Well, I'll try to arrange the schedule, Dr. Stewart.

14
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:43,110
But it's not going to be easy.

15
00:00:43,110 --> 00:00:48,010
I know you'll be able to take care of it.

16
00:00:48,010 --> 00:00:49,430
Well, Mrs. Herrera,

17
00:00:49,430 --> 00:00:53,320
Carl will be perfectly fine after we remove his tonsils.

18
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:55,880
Thank you for your reassurance, Dr. Stewart.

19
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:58,890
He's had so many colds and sore throats recently.

20
00:00:58,890 --> 00:01:01,330
Well, it's a very easy operation, Carl.

21
00:01:01,330 --> 00:01:02,770
You won't feel a thing.

22
00:01:02,770 --> 00:01:05,200
But when do they do it?

23
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:06,690
This Friday.

24
00:01:06,690 --> 00:01:10,030
But Saturday's my birthday.

25
00:01:10,030 --> 00:01:14,740
Well, we could reschedule the operation, Mrs. Herrera,

26
00:01:14,740 --> 00:01:17,360
but I don't want to put it off too long.

27
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:20,460
No, I think it's important to do it now.

28
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:22,260
We can have a birthday party for you, Carl,

29
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:23,760
When you come out of the hospital.

30
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:26,310
But it won't be on my birthday.

31
00:01:26,310 --> 00:01:29,590
But your health is more important, Carl. Believe me.

32
00:01:29,590 --> 00:01:35,310
I don't want my tonsils out.

33
00:01:35,310 --> 00:01:41,970
Nurse Baker, would you come in, please?

34
00:01:41,970 --> 00:01:47,660
Hello, Mrs. Herrera. Hi, Carl, how you doing?

35
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:51,190
I don't want my tonsils out.

36
00:01:51,190 --> 00:01:52,190
Come with me, Carl.

37
00:01:52,190 --> 00:01:59,410
You and I will talk this over.

38
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:01,550
She has a special way with kids.

39
00:02:01,550 --> 00:02:05,730
She sure does.

40
00:02:05,730 --> 00:02:08,460
Carl, does your throat hurt?

41
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:09,640
Yes.

42
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:12,220
OK. Do you want to get better?

43
00:02:12,220 --> 00:02:13,010
Yes.

44
00:02:13,010 --> 00:02:15,820
OK. We want you to get better, too.

45
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:18,060
You'll have your tonsils out tomorrow,

46
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:20,170
and you won't get so many colds anymore.

47
00:02:20,170 --> 00:02:22,770
But if I have my tonsils out tomorrow,

48
00:02:22,770 --> 00:02:25,960
I'll miss my birthday party on Saturday.

49
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:27,260
I know.

50
00:02:27,260 --> 00:02:29,720
It's a problem, isn't it?

51
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:32,710
Let me try to work something out.

52
00:02:32,710 --> 00:02:34,580
What?

53
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:36,220
I have to think about it.

54
00:02:36,220 --> 00:02:37,820
You're fooling me.

55
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:39,810
Oh, I'm not, Carl.

56
00:02:39,810 --> 00:02:41,820
Give me a chance to think about it,

57
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:44,190
and I'll come up with something.

58
00:02:44,190 --> 00:02:45,490
A surprise?

59
00:02:45,490 --> 00:02:46,340
Maybe.

60
00:02:46,340 --> 00:02:48,260
But you just put on your pajamas and robe,

61
00:02:48,260 --> 00:02:51,130
and I'll think of a surprise.

62
00:02:51,130 --> 00:02:52,240
Will it hurt?

63
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:53,060
No.

64
00:02:53,060 --> 00:02:54,470
There are other boys and girls here,

65
00:02:54,470 --> 00:02:55,800
and they're having their tonsils out.

66
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:56,880
You'll meet them.

67
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:59,900
I don't want to.

68
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:01,520
Change your clothes, Carl.

69
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:04,520
Everything will be just fine.
